<node id="&quot;COMUNE DI MILANO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">The COMUNE DI MILANO is the municipal government of Milan, Italy, which plays a multifaceted role in promoting sustainability, social welfare, and community development. As the city council of Milan, it accredits the SFA service and supports SpesaSospesa.org through its collaboration with Terre des Hommes and Banco Alimentare.

The Comune di Milano is also involved in various initiatives aimed at reducing food waste, including the ZeroSprechi protocol and providing space for the hub. In 2021, it won the Earthshot Prize for its anti-food waste policies, which have led to the establishment of the Selinunte Hub as part of its broader food sustainability efforts.

The city government has funded several projects, including the We care project, which supports Ukrainian refugees in collaboration with Fondazione di Comunità Milano. Additionally, it has initiated a fund to support urban farming initiatives, manages the Parco Agricolo Sud Milano, and organizes events like the 'Coltivami' project.

The Comune di Milano is responsible for managing urban gardens, environmental initiatives, and open data platforms. It promotes urban agriculture initiatives and manages community gardens, as well as overseeing the PII (Programma Integrato di Intervento) Greco-Conti initiative.

The municipal authority also supports various food recovery projects, including the Hub Foody Zero Sprechi and collaborates with other organizations on these initiatives. Furthermore, it provides assistance to families in need through the Humus project, which is supported by the Area Food Policy.

The Comune di Milano has initiated and continues to support the Aiuto Alimentare Foody Zero Sprechi project, providing funding and policy backing. It is also involved in various projects such as the Bilancio Partecipativo 2015, the BinG initiative, and the management of public spaces like the CLIMBinG wall and the Area Verde.

The municipal government has collaborated with Fondazione DeBenedetti on poverty-related studies and initiatives, and funds the Nutrire Milano project. It initiated the 'Sistema Milano' project and awarded a bid to Fondazione Bertini for its development.

Lastly, the Comune di Milano oversees the 'Dispositivo Aiuto Alimentare' initiative, collaborating with AMAT, Banco Alimentare della Lombardia, and other organizations to deliver food aid to vulnerable residents.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fea3cf4985647979ea21d1a77872d2b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38562ffdf247d25274b9fa9ce5f44588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61e84d8604999233bc1db00110127184&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7093166ec9031db960ae9954c9f554fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c366ff16a208eea3514b6f96cc2a6833&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09a1c37eba53b08f64e23afd7158368f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9204fe249d282d013a9f1345987f3b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09b5ccbdea171d3d349c4ca3a286fd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bae4ffa887a94a1fc43e0a9f2b13f788&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a69ed15ff5fc7f0697a39021dcd0056&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f3ba68ed55154378509c2dcddbb781&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-474c106969a3b0dbaaddb2047ffd57ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b313e616751bb0128e8116f9c59c56c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5099669bf958d7496fe017b83fc7e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df0c9a719303f6566504d1dbe06790f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee4cc7ed5a47585332175b5c71a8d0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a452466297abd4545528fd86705a442d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-027ad7a66335ba6f33bae532fd9ac624&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-482f7b9d3199c10e4bf282b3774515fc</data>
